CORE
output_port_part_select_driver1.sv
--bound 10
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.counter != 5: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.v != 5: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An output port of a child module connected to a part-select of a parent
net (.o(v[3:0])). The bits of v that the continuous assignment does not
drive are constrained to equal the port in every timeframe.
